// Conformance cases for the three default fonts (docs/default-fonts.adoc):
// Inter, Merriweather and Fira Code, the committed files in package/fonts/
// pinned by SHA-256, at several locations (docs/variable-fonts.adoc §7.2).
//
// A case without `variations`, `variation` or `instance` measures at
// roc-font's default, `Font.Variation.{}` (Regular, `wght` 400): the oracle
// is given every axis explicitly (scripts/_common.py, resolve_location),
// because HarfBuzz's own default is the font's default instance, which is
// Light for Merriweather and Fira Code. `light-default` cases select that
// default instance explicitly.
//
// Kinds: `shape`; `coords` (normalised F2Dot14 coordinates); `advances`
// (per glyph: `.notdef`, the glyphs of a Latin sample, the last glyph);
// `metrics`; `extents` (ink boxes; needs gvar at other locations); `width`
// (Chrome). Driver protocol 1 runs only cases at the font's default
// location (Inter at Regular, Merriweather and Fira Code at Light); the
// rest report `unsupported:location` or `unsupported:kind=<kind>` until the
// driver speaks protocol 2 (docs/conformance.adoc, "The driver").
//
// Generated once; edit by hand from here on. Expectations were filled by
// `record_oracle.py --fill-expected default-fonts` (HarfBuzz 14.6.0, Chrome
// 156); "oracle" marks results too long to repeat here.
{
  "schema": 1,
